  "rationale": "F1 of the flame-reading spec, data-informed (not zero-shot): the numbers of flex_heptane.wsp2 D2, unchanged, with a clock that can be wrong (R1's one number) and the flame cameras switched on. When a prefix carries UV or colour flame diameters, the forward reads one fact from them: whether cameras that recorded this flame still show it at the cutoff. A hot flame is in those traces; a cool flame and an unlit droplet are not. The five numbers of the camera block describe the instrument (frame rates, the ignition flash, how often a flame leaves both views) and were typed from a train-only measurement of the flame traces; none is taken from an outcome of a run, and nothing about the laws was changed. On a prefix without flame diameters the forecast is that of R1. No fit, no search; no validation outcome was read.",
  "origin": "system"
}
